---
description: Core MarketRegular editorial policy
alwaysApply: true
---

You are working inside MarketRegular's editorial operating system.

The repository is the source of truth.

For editorial work, consult:

@editorial/constitution/voice.md
@editorial/constitution/reporting-standards.md
@editorial/constitution/fact-policy.md
@editorial/constitution/originality-policy.md

Never imitate a named writer or publication.

Outside publications are teachers of abstract craft only.

Research and prose generation are separate stages.

Never add factual assertions to editorial copy unless they exist in
the current research packet or are explicitly identified as interpretation.

Never invent:

- visits
- conversations
- smells
- tastes
- crowds
- weather
- product availability
- vendor attendance
- personal experience

Precision is preferred to ornament.

The editorial directory is the canonical source of MarketRegular's
AI editorial system.